harges regarding the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filioque\" target=\"_blank\">Filioque</a> \u2013 philosophical debate in Church if Son was created <i>by</i> Holy Spirit, or <i>created</i> Holy Spirit \u2013 so should Son be praised in prayers ( side of Rome ).<br /> <br /> Methodius vindicated his orthodoxy at Rome, the more easily as the creed was still recited there without the Filioque, and promised to obey in regard to the liturgy. The other party was conciliated by giving him a Swabian, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiching\" target=\"_blank\">Wiching</a>, as his coadjutor. When relations were strained between the two, John VIII steadfastly supported Methodius - but after his death (December 882) the archbishop's position became insecure, and his need of support induced Goetz to accept the statement of the <i>Vita</i> (xiii.) that he went to visit the Eastern emperor.<br /> <br /> It was not until after Methodius' death, which is placed on 6 April 885, that the animosity erupted into an open conflict. Gorazd, whom Methodius had designated as his successor, was not recognized by Pope Stephen V. The same Pope forbade the use of the Slavic liturgy and placed the infamous Wiching as Methodius' successor. The latter exiled the disciples of the two brothers from Great Moravia in 885. They fled to the First Bulgarian Empire, where they were welcomed and commissioned to establish theological schools. There they devised the Cyrillic script on the basis of the Glagolitic. Cyrillic gradually replaced Glagolitic as the alphabet of the Old Church Slavonic language, which became the official language of the Bulgarian Empire and later spread to the Eastern Slav lands of Kievan Rus'. Cyrillic eventually spread throughout most of the Slavic world to become the standard alphabet in the Eastern Orthodox Slavic countries. Hence, Cyril and Methodius' efforts also paved the way for the spread of Christianity throughout Eastern Europe.<br /> <br /> Methodius' body was buried in the main cathedral church of Great Moravia. Until today it remains an open question which city was capital of Great Moravia and therefore the place of Methodius' eternal rest remains unknown. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2018, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T03:19:59-08:00","id":1175406,"title":"","content":"And here is much shorter version of creation of Cyrillic script\u2026<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Invention of the Glagolitic and Cyrillic alphabets</span></b><br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glagolitic_script\" target=\"_blank\">Glagolitic</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyrillic_script\" target=\"_blank\">Cyrillic</a> alphabets are the oldest known Slavic alphabets, and were created by the two brothers and their students, to translate the Bible and other texts into the Slavic languages. The early Glagolitic alphabet was used in Great Moravia between 863 (the arrival of Cyril and Methodius) and 885 (the expulsion of their students) for government and religious documents and books, and at the <b>Great Moravian Academy</b> (Ve\u013ekomoravsk\u00e9 u\u010dili\u0161te) founded by Cyril, where followers of Cyril and Methodius were educated, by Methodius himself among others. The alphabet has been traditionally attributed to Cyril. That attribution has been confirmed explicitly by the papal letter <i>Industriae tuae</i> (880) approving the use of Old Church Slavonic, which says that the alphabet was &quot;invented by Constantine the Philosopher&quot;. The term invention need not exclude the possibility of the brothers having made use of earlier letters, but implies only that before that time the Slavic languages had no distinct script of their own.<br /> <br /> The early Cyrillic alphabet was developed in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Bulgarian_Empire\" target=\"_blank\">First Bulgarian Empire</a> and later finalized and spread by disciples Kliment and Naum in the Ohrid and Preslav schools of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boris_I_of_Bulgaria\" target=\"_blank\">Tsar Boris I</a> of Bulgaria as a simplification of the Glagolitic alphabet which more closely resembled the Greek alphabet. It was developed by the disciples of Saints Cyril and Methodius at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preslav_Literary_School\" target=\"_blank\">Preslav Literary School</a> at the end of the 9th century.<br /> <br /> After the death of Cyril, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clement_of_Ohrid\" target=\"_blank\">Clement of Ohrid</a> accompanied Methodius from Rome to Pannonia and Great Moravia. After the death of Methodius in 885, Clement headed the struggle against the German clergy in Great Moravia along with Gorazd. After spending some time in jail, he was expelled from Great Moravia, and in 885 or 886 reached the borders of the Bulgarian Empire together with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Naum\" target=\"_blank\">Naum</a> of Preslav, Angelarius, and possibly Gorazd (according to other sources, Gorazd was already dead by that time). The four of them were afterwards sent to the Bulgarian capital of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pliska\" target=\"_blank\">Pliska</a>, where they were commissioned by Tsar Boris I of Bulgaria to instruct the future clergy of the state in the Slavonic language.<br /> <br /> After the adoption of Christianity in 865, religious ceremonies in Bulgaria were conducted in Greek by clergy sent from the Byzantine Empire. Fearing growing Byzantine influence and weakening of the state, Boris viewed the adoption of the Old Slavonic language as a way to preserve the political independence and stability of Bulgaria, so he established two literary schools (academies), in Pliska and Ohrid, where theology was to be taught in the Slavonic language. While Naum of Preslav stayed in Pliska working on the foundation of the Pliska Literary School, Clement was commissioned by Boris I to organise the teaching of theology to future clergymen in Old Church Slavonic at the Ohrid Literary School. For seven years (886-893) Clement taught some 3,500 students in the Slavonic language and the Glagolitic alphabet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T04:43:00-08:00","id":1175423,"title":"","content":"So answering one question coming to forward with creation of Cyrillic writing in Bulgaria...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>What language used Byzantine's on day-to-day basis?</b></span><br /> It's complex topic. At beginning, official language of Byzantine Emperor, his court and administration was Latin. But as most of East Roman Empire came from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenization\" target=\"_blank\">Hellenized</a> states, they follow Medieval Greek ( see below ) on day-to-day usage. <b>In 7th century Byzantine Greek becomes official language of Emperor and his court.</b> Latin was still taught on universities to translate texts and communicate with Rome and Pope. From the beginning of 10th century <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Church_Slavonic\" target=\"_blank\">Old Church Slavonic</a> was used by Orthodox Church of Empire in Slavic lands, with simple Cyrillic script.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Medieval Greek</span></b><br /> Medieval Greek, also known as <i>Byzantine Greek</i>, is the stage of the Greek language between the end of Classical antiquity in the 5th\u20136th centuries and the end of the Middle Ages, conventionally dated to the Ottoman conquest of Constantinople in 1453.<br /> <br /> The beginning of Medieval Greek is occasionally dated back to as early as the 4th century, either to 330 AD, when the political centre of the Roman Empire was moved to Constantinople, or to 395 AD, the division of the Empire. However, this approach is rather arbitrary as it is more an assumption of political, as opposed to cultural and linguistic, developments. Indeed, by this time the spoken language, particularly pronunciation, had already shifted towards modern forms. At first, Latin remained the language of both the court and the army and it was used for official documents, but its influence soon waned. From the beginning of the 6th century, amendments to the law were mostly written in Greek.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, parts of the Roman <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corpus_Juris_Civilis\" target=\"_blank\">Corpus Iuris Civilis</a> were gradually translated into Greek. Under the rule of Emperor <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclius\" target=\"_blank\">Heraclius</a> (610\u2013641 AD), who also assumed the Greek title <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basileus\" target=\"_blank\">Basileus</a> (Greek: \u03b2\u03b1\u03c3\u03b9\u03bb\u03b5\u03cd\u03c2, &quot;monarch&quot;) in 629, Greek became the official language of the Eastern Roman Empire. This was in spite of the fact that the inhabitants of the empire still considered themselves Romaioi (&quot;Romans&quot;) until its end in 1453.<br /> <br /> From the 7th century onwards, Greek was the only language of administration and government in the Byzantine Empire. This stage of language is thus described as Byzantine Greek. The study of the Medieval Greek language and literature is a branch of Byzantine Studies, or Byzantinology, the study of the history and culture of the Byzantine Empire.<br /> <br /> Despite the absence of reliable demographic figures, it has been estimated that less than one third of the inhabitants of the Eastern Roman Empire, around eight million people, were native speakers of Greek. The number of those who were able to communicate in Greek may have been far higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2018, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T06:05:13-08:00","id":1175431,"title":"","content":"<b>CoD Factions names translated to Greek</b><br /> So as Byzantine Empire change his official language to Greek in 7<sup>th</sup> century, I suspect most of Latin-based names of monsters factions will be translated. Here are vampires Covenants of this Era.<br /> <br /> <b>Invictus</b> - A\u00edttiti<br /> <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> - Ag\u00eda Lans<br /> <b>Legio Mortem</b> - Lege\u00f3na Metathan\u00e1tia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T06:24:58-08:00","id":1175435,"title":"","content":"And here we have article on the education in the Byzantine Empire...<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Education in Byzantium</span></b><br /> Byzantine education was the product of an ancient Greek educational tradition that stretched back to the 5th century BC. It comprised a tripartite system of education that, taking shape during the Hellenistic era, was maintained, with inevitable changes, up until the fall of Constantinople. The stages of education were the elementary school, where pupils ranged from six to ten years, secondary school, where pupils ranged from ten to sixteen, and higher education.<br /> Elementary education was widely available throughout most of the Byzantine Empire's existence, in towns and occasionally in the countryside. This, in turn, ensured that literacy was much more widespread than in Western Europe, at least until the twelfth century. Secondary education was confined to the larger cities while higher education was the exclusive provenance of Constantinople.<br /> Though not a society of mass literacy like modern societies, Byzantine society was a profoundly literate one. Based on information from an extensive array of Byzantine documents from different periods (i.e. homilies, Ecloga, etc.), Robert Browning concluded that, while books were luxury items and functional literacy (reading and writing) was widespread, but largely confined to cities and monasteries, access to elementary education was provided in most cities for much of the time and sometimes in villages. Nikolaos Oikonomides, focusing on 13th-century Byzantine literacy in Western Asia Minor, states that Byzantine society had &quot;a completely literate church, an almost completely literate aristocracy, some literate horsemen, rare literate peasants and almost completely illiterate women.&quot; Ioannis Stouraitis estimates that the percentage of the Empire's population with some degree of literacy was at most 15\u201320% based primarily on the mention of illiterate Byzantine tourmarchai in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tactica_of_Emperor_Leo_VI_the_Wise\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tactica</i></a> of Emperor Leo VI the Wise (r. 886\u2013912).<br /> In Byzantium, the elementary school teacher occupied a low social position and taught mainly from simple fairy tale books (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aesop%27s_Fables\" target=\"_blank\">Aesop's Fables</a> were often used). However, the grammarian and rhetorician, teachers responsible for the following two phases of education, were more respected. These used classical Greek texts like Homer's Iliad or Odyssey and much of their time was taken with detailed word-for-word explication. Books were rare and very expensive and likely only possessed by teachers who dictated passages to students.<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b> With education high, but literacy still less than half of population like in 19th and 20th century Europe - Byzantine characters that want to read and write need to buy this Merit:<br /> <br /> <b>Literate (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prequsition:</b> Intelligence 2+<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Before public education system ( for example, from 1833 in England ) literacy was part of only small percent of population. Even educated people not always were able to read. This Merit marks character as able to read and write in all Languages she knows and her homeland tongue. Characters with <i>Multilingual</i> Merit may read or write in those languages, but need to do Intelligence+Academics rolls for this.<br /> <b>Note:</b> If Storyteller allows this Merit, he should ban <i>Illiterate</i> Persistence Condition in the same Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-12-2018, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T08:05:52-08:00","id":1176286,"title":"","content":"Question on Vampire part of Byzantium setting - <b>WHEN falling Senex Wing become Invictus?</b> I cannot seem to find it in <b>Requiem for Rome</b> and <b>Fall of Camarilla</b>... Books show that Lancea Sanctum and Legio Mortuum simply just transferred to Constantinopole - but there is nothing on rise of Invictus. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> could help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-15-2018, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T08:24:13-08:00","id":1176291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1176286#post1176286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on Vampire part of Byzantium setting - <b>WHEN falling Senex Wing become Invictus?</b> I cannot seem to find it in <b>Requiem for Rome</b> and <b>Fall of Camarilla</b>... Books show that Lancea Sanctum and Legio Mortuum simply just transferred to Constantinopole - but there is nothing on rise of Invictus. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> could help?</div> </div> </div> </div>See Ancient Mysteries. There are 2 &quot;Invictus&quot; during that time, actually- one in Byzantium and the other in the Germanic lands (I can't remember their name or exact timeline). Eventually, the German covenant would destroy and devour the Byzantium one, and the Invictus would be born from the outcome.<br /> <br /> Checked for the dates. The Die Unbesiegt were officially founded at 1142AD, after a Ventrue german lord after he met with the surviving members of the Senex in Rome. The Athanatoi of Byzantium are the direct descendants of the Camarilla in the Eastern Roman Empire. In 1204, when Boniface conquered the city in the fourth crusade, the Lancea et Sanctum and the rising Invictus came with the army and destroyed every member of the covenant which they could find, leaving one and only Invictus to rule over the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-15-2018, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T09:19:05-08:00","id":1176301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1176291#post1176291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1204, when Boniface conquered the city in the fourth crusade, the Lancea et Sanctum and the rising Invictus came with the army and destroyed every member of the covenant which they could find, leaving one and only Invictus to rule over the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, wait - So Germanic 'Invictus' ( Die Unbesiegt ) with Germanic Lancea Sanctum destroyed all Byzantine 'heretics' of their respective Covenants in Constantinople, on Fourth Crusade? So, in Kindred circles, vampires of Byzantium fall in 1204, not with rest of Empire in 1453 A.D.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T09:30:42-08:00","id":1176302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1176301#post1176301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, wait - So Germanic 'Invictus' ( Die Unbesiegt ) with Germanic Lancea Sanctum destroyed all Byzantine 'heretics' of their respective Covenants in Constantinople, on Fourth Crusade? So, in Kindred circles, vampires of Byzantium fall in 1204, not with rest of Empire in 1453 A.D.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T11:24:54-08:00","id":1176333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1176286#post1176286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on Vampire part of Byzantium setting - <b>WHEN falling Senex Wing become Invictus?</b> I cannot seem to find it in <b>Requiem for Rome</b> and <b>Fall of Camarilla</b>... Books show that Lancea Sanctum and Legio Mortuum simply just transferred to Constantinopole - but there is nothing on rise of Invictus. Maybe <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> could help?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Wyrd, I\u2019ve basically quit thse forums, and no longer play CofD.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T12:36:19-08:00","id":1176569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1176291#post1176291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See Ancient Mysteries. There are 2 &quot;Invictus&quot; during that time, actually- one in Byzantium and the other in the Germanic lands (I can't remember their name or exact timeline). Eventually, the German covenant would destroy and devour the Byzantium one, and the Invictus would be born from the outcome.<br /> <br /> Checked for the dates. The Die Unbesiegt were officially founded at 1142AD, after a Ventrue german lord after he met with the surviving members of the Senex in Rome. The Athanatoi of Byzantium are the direct descendants of the Camarilla in the Eastern Roman Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side question - So what's with Camarilla left overs <i>before</i> Die Unbesiegt creation? There were no protoInvictus ideas in Europe before 1142AD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T13:37:18-08:00","id":1176588,"title":"","content":"Some of the Senex has survived, so some ideas may have survived- but as a Covenant, the Athanatoi were the strongest power house in Europe. I imagine that the Senex were just too bust at licking their wounds in Rome, closing themselves in a much more isolated region and imagining that maybe they have some of the glory they once had in the ages past. As far as the Kindred are concerned (and not only them), Europe is broken and bleeding after the fall of Rome, and with the once eternal Camarilla being shattered into so many pieces, it would take years beforte someone would be willing to endanger himself and touch those sharp, broken shards. According to Ancient Mysteries, the Athanatoi are the &quot;Invictus&quot; of that Era- and it is their lack of vision and clinging to ages old traditions which have already rotten away is what that brought their downfall. They simply couldn't believe that Some other group would manage to gather the leftovers of the Camarilla, their ideas and goals, and make something new. Oh, they probably knew about the Senex- but they could believe that someone would manage to make those geezers to actually do something. They were sure of their power and place in their world, because there was no real threat to their power. That was their mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T21:17:54-08:00","id":1176686,"title":"","content":"But the aristocratic vampires are all over the Europe, without Athanatoi influance? Most of Western and Center Europe's kingdoms - like Catalonia, France, Great Moravia or even my homeland Poland - till year 900, max 1000 are rebuild states, based on Christian Aristocracy and Clerygy model through out Europe. It's just hard to image for me that there will be no Aristocratic vampires in Charles the Great and later Frankish court in Paris, for example. Or that first three Crusades would not have Invictus like sponsors. Remember that exchange with Byzantine Empire is really limited, even after Vikings 'discovery' of the Silk Road - so Athanatoi would not spread all over Europe from Constantinopole. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-17-2018, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T22:46:11-08:00","id":1176699,"title":"","content":"It's not that there are no local Princes- but something in the scale of the Invictus simply doesn't emerge during that time and place. As I said- the Senex still exist, simply contained to Rome and without any real power. The Lance and the Legion are the powers which control Western Europe during that time, not to mention the Gallows Post. The Invictus is not &quot;aristocratic vampires&quot;- it is a conspiracy, an empire, and a covenant which is able to collect all of those powerful Kindred and unite them into a single front is something which would not exist until much later. You can change it, if you want- but as far as current canon is concerned, that's the situation. The vampire society is in trauma after the Fall of the Camarilla, and the Lance used the opportunity to take over their assets and become the major power the the region. No matter how hard did humanity took the fall of Rome, the Kindred too it much harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T02:00:43-08:00","id":1176725,"title":"","content":"As we are at religious matters in Byzantine Empire, let\u2019s talk about\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Creation of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Orthodox_Churchhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Orthodox_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Orthodox Church</a> </b></span><br /> From the iconoclast <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Hieria\" target=\"_blank\">Council of Hieria in 754</a> - called by Byzantium Emperor that wanted to ban icons worship in the area of Empire \u2013 rose tension between Pope in Rome and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecumenical_Patriarch_of_Constantinople\" target=\"_blank\">Patriarch of Constantinople</a> about then One Church influence in Byzantium.<br /> <br /> When <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Council_of_Nicaea\" target=\"_blank\">Second Council of Nicaea in 787</a> reverted the rulings from Hieria, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecclesiastical_differences_between_the_Catholic_Church_and_the_Eastern_Orthodox_Church\" target=\"_blank\">Church </a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecclesiastical_differences_between_the_Catholic_Church_and_the_Eastern_Orthodox_Church)\" target=\"_blank\">governing differences</a> rose. With added changing in Byzantium <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1175423#post1175423\">usage of Latin to Greek in official matters</a> \u2013 and slow creation of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Rite\" target=\"_blank\">Byzantine Rite of liturgy</a> ( also known as Greek Rite ) by this \u2013 the two Churches started to split, even if technically all of future Orthodox Church was in 9<sup>th</sup> and 10<sup>th</sup> century still under government of Pope from Rome. Remember that even now Orthodox Church Patriarch of Constantinople is <i>de facto </i>only one of Archbishops in synod \u2013 even if he is treated as \u2018spiritual leader\u2019 of East Church, titled <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primus_inter_pares\" target=\"_blank\"><i>primus inter pares</i></a> (first among equals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2018, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T02:21:56-08:00","id":1176727,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photian_schism\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Photian Schism of 863 \u2013 867</b></span></a><br /> In 858 layman Photius supporting young <a href=\"http://https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_III\" target=\"_blank\">Emperor Micheal III</a> ( he was only 18 years old then ) was elected in place of previous Patriarch \u2013 Ingatius - and was hurriedly consecrated bishop within one week contrary to the canonical rules but not without precedent in Constantinople. After some tensions with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Nicholas_I\" target=\"_blank\">Pope Nicholas I</a>, Pope reinstated Ingatius on synod of 863 in Rome.<br /> <br /> Much of conflict between Rome and Constantinople rose over centuries from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filioque\" target=\"_blank\">Filioque issue</a> \u2013 that in short, is question does Jesus is god that created Holy Spirit. In 865 First Bulgar Empire had accepted Christianity from the Byzantines after a short war that resulted in conversion <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boris_I_of_Bulgaria\" target=\"_blank\">Kniaz Boris I</a> and promise to convert his people. On meeting refusal from Photius for a separate patriarch for these new Christians, Boris had invited Latin missionaries from Rome. In 867, Photius attacked these Latins for adding the Filioque to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicene_Creed\" target=\"_blank\">Nicene Creed</a>. He did not make this accusation against the Western Church as whole, still less against Rome, which at that time had not accepted this addition to the Creed. Only in the late 13th century, when the Filioque was central to Byzantine polemics, were his arguments adopted, and few had even referred to them until then.<br /> <br /> With the approval of the Emperor, who feared what was seen as an advance of the Franks close to his capital, Photius invited the patriarchs of Alexandria, Antioch and Jerusalem to meet in Constantinople and pronounce on this &quot;encroachment&quot;. This 867 synod took the grave step of condemning Pope Nicholas as a heretic and declaring him deposed.<br /> <br /> Kniaz Boris I of Bulgaria would further complicate relations between Rome and Constantinople by approaching Pope Nicholas. Photius was aware of Boris's approaches and sought to ease his mind on how to be a Christian Leader by writing, 'On the Duties of a prince'. Boris had also asked the Pope 115 questions, which Pope Nicholas answered in <i>Responsa Nicolai papae I. ad consulta Bulgarorum</i> (The Responses of Pope Nicholas I to the Questions of the Bulgars). However, due to the popes refusal to appoint Formosus as archbishop of Bulgaria, the kniaz once again turned to Byzantium, who granted Bulgaria autocephalous status during the 4th council of Constantinople.<br /> <br /> Nicholas died before news of this action reached Rome. In the same year, Emperor Michael III was killed, and his murderer and successor <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil_I\" target=\"_blank\">Basil I</a> deposed Photius, replacing him by Ignatius. After the death or deposition of the two protagonists, their successors reestablished communion, thus ending the schism, though not the disputes between the two sees.<br /> <br /> Ignatius upheld Byzantine claims to Bulgaria no less strongly than Photius. And when he died in 877, Photius was made patriarch again. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_John_VIII\" target=\"_blank\">Pope John VIII</a> was more flexible than Nicholas I and at a council in Constantinople in 879\u2013880 his legates confirmed acceptance of Photius as patriarch and agreed to an arrangement whereby Rome was given nominal authority over Bulgaria but actual jurisdiction was in the hands of Constantinople. Bulgaria would remain autocephalous until 927, when it would be elevated to a Patriarchate during Peace accords with the Byzantine Empire.<br /> <br /> Further north than Bulgaria, in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Moravia\" target=\"_blank\">Greater Moravia</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1175398#post1175398\">Saints Cyril and Methodius</a>, who had been sent by Emperor Michael and Photius, sided with the Pope against Photius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T02:26:57-08:00","id":1176728,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">10th and 11th century West-East Church problems</span></b><br /> The 10th century relations between Pope in Roma and Patriarch of Constantinople were very tense. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filioque\" target=\"_blank\">Filioque issue</a> \u2013 that in short, is question does Jesus is god that created Holy Spirit. <span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clerical_celibacy_(Catholic_Church)#Historical_origins\" target=\"_blank\">celibacy of priests</a></span><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> were often risen on various synods. It is sometimes claimed that celibacy became mandatory for Latin Church priests only in the eleventh century; but others say, for instance: &quot;(I)t may fairly be said that by the time of St. Leo the Great (440\u201361) the law of celibacy was generally recognized in the West,&quot; and that the eleventh-century regulations on this matter, as on simony (selling churches offices and roles ), should obviously not be interpreted as meaning that either non-celibacy or simony were previously permitted.</span><br /> <br /> &quot;Despite six hundred years of decrees, canons, and increasingly harsh penalties, the Latin clergy still did, more or less illegally, what their Greek counterparts were encouraged to do by law\u2014they lived with their wives and raised families. In practice, ordination was not an impediment to marriage; therefore some priests did marry even after ordination. The tenth century is claimed to be the high point of clerical marriage in the Latin communion. Most rural priests were married and many urban clergy and bishops had wives and children. A terrible picture of the decay both of clerical morality and of all sense of anything like vocation is drawn in the writings of St. Peter Damian, particularly in his <i>Liber Gomorrhianus</i>. The style, no doubt, is rhetorical and exaggerated, and his authority as an eyewitness does not extend beyond that district of Northern Italy, in which he lived, but we have evidence from other sources that the corruption was widespread\u2026 Undoubtedly during this period the traditions of sacerdotal celibacy in Western Christendom suffered severely but even though a large number of the clergy, not only priests but bishops, openly took wives and begot children to whom they transmitted their benefices, the principle of celibacy was never completely surrendered in the official enactments of the Church.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 888, two local councils, that of Metz and that of Mainz, prohibited cohabitation even with wives living in continence. This tendency was taken up by the 11th-century <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_Reform\" target=\"_blank\">Gregorian Reform</a> (c. 1050\u201380), which aimed at eliminating what it called &quot;Nicolaitism&quot;, that is clerical marriage, which in spite of being theoretically excluded was in fact practised, and concubinage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T02:30:22-08:00","id":1176729,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East%E2%80%93West_Schism\" target=\"_blank\">Great Schism of 1054</a> and it\u2019s repercussions</span></b><br /> In 1053, the first step was taken in the process which led to formal schism between West and East Church. The Greek churches in southern Italy were forced either to close or to conform to Latin practices. In retaliation, the Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_I_Cerularius\" target=\"_blank\">Michael I Cerularius</a> ordered the closure of all Latin churches in Constantinople. In 1054, the papal legate sent by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_IX\" target=\"_blank\">Leo IX</a> travelled to Constantinople for purposes that included refusing to Cerularius the title of &quot;Ecumenical Patriarch&quot; and insisting that he recognize the Pope's claim to be the head of all the churches. The main purpose of the papal legation was to seek help from the Byzantine Emperor in view of the Norman conquest of southern Italy and to deal with recent attacks by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_of_Ohrid\" target=\"_blank\">Leo of Ohrid</a> against the use of unleavened bread and other Western customs, attacks that had the support of Cerularius. Historian Axel Bayer says the legation was sent in response to two letters, one from the Emperor seeking assistance in arranging a common military campaign by the eastern and western empires against the Normans, and the other from Cerularius. On the refusal of Cerularius to accept the demand, the leader of the legation, Cardinal Humbert of Silva Candida, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/O.S.B.\" target=\"_blank\">O.S.B.</a>, excommunicated him, and in return Cerularius excommunicated Humbert and the other legates. This was only the first act in a centuries-long process that eventually became a complete schism.<br /> <br /> The validity of the Western legates' act is doubtful, since Leo had died and Cerularius' excommunication applied only to the legates personally. Still, the Church split and the fundamental breach has never been healed, with each side sometimes accusing the other of having fallen into heresy and of having initiated the division. Later Crusades, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massacre_of_the_Latins\" target=\"_blank\">Massacre of the Latins</a> in 1182, the West's retaliation in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sack_of_Thessalonica_(1185)\" target=\"_blank\">Sacking of Thessalonica</a> in 1185, the capture and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Constantinople_(1203)\" target=\"_blank\">Siege of Constantinople</a> in 1203, and the imposition of Latin patriarchs made reconciliation more difficult. Establishing Latin hierarchies in the Crusader states meant that there were two rival claimants to each of the patriarchal sees of Antioch, Constantinople, and Jerusalem, making the existence of schism clear. Several attempts at reconciliation did not bear fruit. In 1965, Pope Paul VI and the Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople Athenagoras I nullified the anathemas of 1054, although this nullification of measures taken against a few individuals was essentially a goodwill gesture and did not constitute any sort of reunion. Contacts between the two sides continue: every year a delegation from each joins in the other's celebration of its patronal feast, Saints Peter and Paul (29 June) for Rome and Saint Andrew (30 November) for Constantinople, and there have been a number of visits by the head of each to the other. The efforts of the Ecumenical Patriarchs towards reconciliation with the Catholic Church have often been the target of sharp criticism from some fellow Orthodox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T17:58:25-08:00","id":1176868,"title":"","content":"I feel like I am back in my old history courses here, albeit with less aegumentation. Ah, the wonders of a medievalist background...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5435-mhicwombat","name":"MhicWombat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T13:14:35-08:00","id":1183031,"title":"","content":"I've found <a href=\"http://www.byzantium1200.com/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">this very cool site</a> with a 3d model of Constantinople in 1200 A.D. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T04:51:13-08:00","id":1274174,"title":"","content":"Returning after long time no writing - but probably with new cool ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Plague of Justinian (541\u2013542 AD)</a> is now canonically in <b>CoD</b> one of historical instances of Contagion ( from <b>Contagion Chronicles</b> ) that also cemented Jeremiad Sworn faction - and with previous <b>Requiem for Rome</b> pointing that it's time Lancea Sanctum took power in Constantinople - I think I would base setting on Sworn groups alliances from <b>CC</b>, rather than classical each races splats only split.<br /> <br /> Then we have historic Sworn split over monster races respond to Contagion in Justinian times, that became de facto 'monstrous parliament', kinda similar to Camarilla of Rome, but limited only to Byzantium and connecting to <b>all</b> monsters in Empire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And it\u2019s cross factions idea is to stop next Contagion to show up in area, that returned in small portions till 8th century. This system all start to break down with passing centuries and not seeing next great Contagion up to the disintegration of Eastern Roman Empire itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 'wings' - i.e. Sworn - would be:<ul><li><b><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jeremiad-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Jeremiad</a> </b>- Religious and morality centered monsters. Connected to mortal ( future ) Orthodox Church. After 6<sup>th</sup> century \u2013 most influential Sworn faction. \u2013 <b>Typical members splats:</b> Lancea Sanctum, Iron Masters, Storm Lords, Silver Ladder, all Beasts following Dark Mother.</li> <li><b><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptocracy</a></b> \u2013 Monsters sustaining government and rules in society. They are left-overs from original Camarilla of Rome. Connected mostly to Eastern Roman Emperor\u2019s court. - <b>Typical members splats:</b> Athanatoi ( rests of Camarilla, future Invictus ), Ivory Claws, Guardians of the Veil, Seers of Throne, Winter Courtiers.</li> <li><b>Ship of Theseus</b> \u2013 \u2018Contagion is evolution\u2019</li> <li><b>Rosetta Society</b> \u2013 Rosetta believe Contagion to be a message from another world which someone has to decipher ( Probably ) \u2013 As Rosetta Stone is from 196 BC from area of Hellenistic Egypt \u2013 I can see their existence in Byzantium era.</li> <li><b>Zero Hour</b> ? ( Probably not, as they are probably too modern to be in Eastern Roman Empire times )</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-14-2018, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T05:22:19-08:00","id":1274177,"title":"","content":"With the Justinian Plague, we can easily see connection of werewolves, joining with vampire and mages fights against epidemic \u2013 especially from Hunters in Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>\u2018According to contemporary sources, the outbreak in Constantinople was thought to have been carried to the city by infected rats on grain ships arriving from Egypt. To feed its citizens, the city and outlying communities imported large amounts of grain, mostly from Egypt. Grain ships may have been the original source of contagion, as the rat (and flea) population in Egypt thrived on feeding from the large granaries maintained by the government. The Byzantine historian Procopius first reported the epidemic in 541 from the port of Pelusium, near Suez in Egypt. Two other firsthand reports of the plague's ravages were by the Syriac church historian John of Ephesus and Evagrius Scholasticus, who was a child in Antioch at the time and later became a church historian. Evagrius was afflicted with the buboes associated with the disease but survived. During the disease's four returns in his lifetime, he lost his wife, a daughter and her child, other children, most of his servants and people from his country estate.\u2019</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T06:16:12-08:00","id":1274183,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Virulence and mortality rate of </span></b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Justinian Plague</span></b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>'The number of deaths is uncertain. Modern scholars believe that the plague killed up to 5,000 people per day in Constantinople at the peak of the pandemic. The initial plague ultimately killed perhaps 40% of the city's inhabitants and caused the deaths of up to a quarter of the human population of the Eastern Mediterranean. Frequent subsequent waves of the plague continued to strike throughout the 6th, 7th and 8th centuries, with the disease becoming more localized and less virulent.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>After the last recurrence in 750, pandemics on the scale of Plague of Justinian did not appear again in Europe until the Black Death of the 14th century.'</i></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T20:04:38-07:00","id":1300455,"title":"","content":"With <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/contagion-chronicle-a-chronicles-of-darkness-cross\" target=\"_blank\">Contagion Chronicle Kickstarter now</a> \u2013 and seeing the previews of book \u2013 I revision Sworn and False for this Dark Era.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Sworn and False of Byzantine Empire</span></b><br /> In brackets are names for modern counterparts of those groups. Historical factions use mechanics the same as their nowadays decedents.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sworn of this Era:</span></b><ul><li><i><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jeremiad-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jeremiad</b></a></i> - Religious and morality centered monsters. Connected to mortal ( future ) Orthodox Church. After 6th century and it\u2019s Plauge of Justinian \u2013 most influential Sworn faction. <b>Typical members:</b> Lancea Sanctum, Iron Masters, Storm Lords, Silver Ladder, all Beasts following Dark Mother.</li> <li><b><i>Athanatoi </i></b>(<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptocracy</a>) \u2013 Monsters sustaining government and rules in society. They are left-overs from original Camarilla of Rome. Connected mostly to Eastern Roman Emperor\u2019s court and army. - <b>Typical members:</b> Athanatoi Convenant ( rests of Camarilla, future Invictus ), Ivory Claws, Guardians of the Veil, Seers of Throne, Winter &amp; Spring Courtiers. Also martial monsters, like Blood Talons, Adamantine Arrow or Summer Court. ( See below why. )</li> <li><b><i>Omphalos</i></b> (Rosetta Society) \u2013 Researches of sacred and secret, they name comes both title for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omphalos\" target=\"_blank\">mythological stone letting to communicate directly with gods</a> \u2013 and Astral Space barrier that many mages and beasts find in their journeys. <b>Typical members: </b>mages from Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates Orders ( in 12<sup>th</sup> century they merge into modern Mysterium, but in this Dark Eras they compete inside Sworn ), beasts, Mekhet vampires.</li> </ul>Zero Hour do not have it\u2019s direct representation as Byzantine army was strictly connected to administrative rulers, dividing Empire into <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_army#The_Themata\" target=\"_blank\">Themata</a>. Many generals and soldiers are part of Athanatoi Sworn, even when they use sometimes they own made Intel Vector. But, for time being, all night-dwellers martial groups join Athanatoi.<br /> <br /> <b>False of this Era:</b><ul><li><i><b>Horde </b></i>(Naglfar\u2019s Army) \u2013 Literal \u2018barbarians at the gates\u2019 \u2013 and on the inside. Over centuries, Easter Roman Empire had many enemies \u2013 Huns, Khazars, Arabs, Vikings, Ottamans and many, many others. Each of this groups was coming with next war that could \u2018end the world\u2019. What was joining them was secret support of night-dwellers, wanting to tear down Empire, once and for all. However Horde was not only on the outside \u2013 but was infiltrating Night Society in the inside. From the times of Ancient Rome, at least handful of monsters were doing their own \u2018Saturnalia\u2019, preparing for the end of world. With enemies on the outside and inside \u2013 Byzantine Empire finally was no more. In 900\u2019s Horde dogma mixed with Vikings legends of Ragnarok \u2013 and modern Naglfar\u2019s Army was created from there.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-28-2019, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:30:58-07:00","id":1300484,"title":"","content":"There is interesting implication of this Sworn factions spread - most of Mage Orders ( with Seers counted ) and most of Seasonal Courts of Changeling ( Winter, Spring and Summer ) are in the <b><i>Athanatoi </i></b> - and they all cooperate in sustaining the Empire, but also compete with each other. The only left are Keepers of the Word with Pancryptiates in <b><i>Omphalos</i></b> - and Autumn Court that, probably, will be split in two - those that are more interested in 'moral lessons' will come to <b><i>Jeremiad</i></b>. Those Autumn Courtiers interest in knowledge will come to <i><b>Omphalos</b></i>. It's also interesting that most influential after Plague is <b><i>Jeremiad</i></b> - when with the largest number is <b><i>Athanatoi</i></b>. But later are fighting constantly inside of them, so it has reasons. <br /> <br /> <b>I still don't have idea where Tremere - as Pentacle Order in that time - should gravitate to.</b> Maybe Jeremiad, as they look for 'immoral' mages?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire#post1137216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">History of Awakend topic</a>, based on <b>Left Hand Path</b> book:<br /> <br /> '<b>8th century AD: Tremere join Diamond - </b>In Eastern Europe, one or two Tremere demanded hospitality at Diamond wizards\u2019 towers. Quickly follow them whole cabals, showing carcasses of monsters they fought to assure good intentions. Tremere were warrior-sorcerers and students of the soul who promised to lead the Awakened to a new age of splendor, built on the ashes of burning enemies. They hunted Seers and Scelesti, but demand selected Reapers and vampires as tribute for the balance of their wrath. They preached that Atlantis\u2019s faithful willworkers were the natural lords of souls. Anyone who challenged their crowns deserved to burn. '<br /> <br /> '<b>1099:</b> <b>Banishment of Tremere</b> - Silver Ladder lictor Caterine Bedlam told the Convocation of Antioch what many now suspected: the Tremere was a Legacy of Reapers who hunted their own kind. It labeled them as Nefandi by Convocation, with banishment and \u2018forgetting\u2019 of Tremere Order members \u2013 their magical tools were destroyed, as any grimoires, soul stones, or imbued items they created. Their Shadow Name becomes illegal to utter and were replaced in all Consilium records by \u201cNefandi:\u201d the name that is not a name and cannot be spoken. As other Convocations followed move that of Antioch done, within few decades Tremere were officially excommunicated from Diamond be every European Convocations, becoming target for Reaper hunters they ones been.'</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T09:30:20-07:00","id":1300566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300484#post1300484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is interesting implication of this Sworn factions spread - most of Mage Orders ( with Seers counted ) and most of Seasonal Courts of Changeling ( Winter, Spring and Summer ) are in the <b><i>Athanatoi </i></b> - and they all cooperate in sustaining the Empire, but also compete with each other. The only left are Keepers of the Word with Pancryptiates in <b><i>Omphalos</i></b> - and Autumn Court that, probably, will be split in two - those that are more interested in 'moral lessons' will come to <b><i>Jeremiad</i></b>. Those Autumn Courtiers interest in knowledge will come to <i><b>Omphalos</b></i>. It's also interesting that most influential after Plague is <b><i>Jeremiad</i></b> - when with the largest number is <b><i>Athanatoi</i></b>. But later are fighting constantly inside of them, so it has reasons.<br /> <br /> <b>I still don't have idea where Tremere - as Pentacle Order in that time - should gravitate to.</b> Maybe Jeremiad, as they look for 'immoral' mages?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In all likelihood, it is individuals who who'll gravitate towards difference sects of the Sworn and the False, not entire factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-28-2019, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T10:03:02-07:00","id":1300582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300566#post1300566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I all likelyhood, it is individuals who who'll gravitate towards difference sects of the Sworn and the False, not entire factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth is spoken here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:34:01-07:00","id":1300636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300566#post1300566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all likelihood, it is individuals who who'll gravitate towards difference sects of the Sworn and the False, not entire factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but stereotypes are made on some basis. Like, most Blood Talons will be in factions related to military or para-military types. So some generalization are to be made in setting building, to see how situation looks like, in broad strokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:27:34-07:00","id":1300669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300636#post1300636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but stereotypes are made on some basis. Like, most Blood Talons will be in factions related to military or para-military types. So some generalization are to be made in setting building, to see how situation looks like, in broad strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the problem is that there's a lot of ways that person might take that an interpret it in any crossover sort of situation, nevermind in context of the Contagion.<br /> <br /> Like, going with the Blood Talon, it's easy to read them as going Zero Hour, thanks to Protagonist Warrior cast, buuuuuut <br /> <br /> Any Talon that is concerned with the betterment of themselves into being an Apex Predator will have cause to be in the Ship of THeseus.<br /> Any Talon that has an abundance of humanity in their pack and considers their wellbeing something to govern over has cause to be in the Cryptocracy.<br /> Any Talon who considers the Contagion who can reasonably consider it's warp and weft an affront to Moon and Wolf has cause to be in the Jeremiad.<br /> Any Talon who thinks that their's no action too drastic against winning against the Contagion has cause to be in the Crucible Initiative.<br /> Any Talon whose willing to win against foes that challenge them and their pack no matter the cost has cause to be in the Machiavelli Gambit.<br /> Any Talon who thinks this is the end of days and is willing to exploit that to emerge the victor in the new world against ancient foes has cause to be in Naglfar's Army.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure if I thought about it, I could answer why a Blood Talon would join the Rosetta Society.<br /> <br /> A Blood Talon will always have prediliections, but what they think being a Blood Talon means and how one should go about it, who makes up their pack, who are their enemies, how they feel about others and whether their character matters more than their actions or not, if they are concerned with the Contagion or not and how much-all of these things will speak to which faction they might join (if they join one at all!) as much if not more so than the mere fact that they are a Blood Talon.<br /> <br /> THe Factions care about attitudes towards the Contagions and unifying means of problem solving. If the Contagion is not a thing in the game you are running, then Factions are basically organizations of monsters who are united by <i>how they deal with problems</i> and not by the <i>ideology that directs those actions</i>. Such things will largely come down to the local politics and ideas of that bit of the Faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:33:52-07:00","id":1300673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300669#post1300669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure if I thought about it, I could answer why a Blood Talon would join the Rosetta Society.</div> </div> </div> </div>All werewolves place high esteem on the importance of tales and the First Tongue, so each and every Auspice, Tribe, and Lodge has a really damn good reason to join the Rosetta Society. Ditto with all Mages and all Demons.<br /> <br /> Or... <br /> <br /> *Hears NDA ninjas land on the roof*<br /> <br /> Or [REDACTED]. I'll circle back to this when I can talk about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T14:42:55-07:00","id":1300677,"title":"","content":"What <i>are</i> they feeding them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:14:00-07:00","id":1301942,"title":"","content":"With Vectors chapter preview we have official spread of monster groups for modern Sworn and False. As I pointed I want for the Byzantine Era groups to be partial different \u2013 but having logical connections to those \u2013 I will repost sum up of modern Sworn spreads to compare them with mine ideas for Byzantine Sworns.<br /> <br /> Modern Sworns from Contagion Chronicle preview:<ul><li>Cryptocrats \u2013 Authority Vector \u2013 Typical members are: beasts, demons, mages and vampires. Joins them Winter Court, Cheiron Group, Task Force: Valkyrie, Maa-Kep, and Undertakers from Sin-Eaters.</li> <li>Jeremiad \u2013 Frevor Vector \u2013 Typical members are: beasts, hunters, mumies and Prometheans. Joins them Integrators, Lancea et Sanctum, Long Night, Lucifuge, and Malleus Maleficarum</li> <li>Rosetta Society \u2013 Semiotics Vector \u2013 Typical members are: mages, demons, changelings, hunters and werewolves. Joins too them Circle of the Crone, Sesha-Hebsu, Mourners from Sin-Eaters and Tammuz.</li> <li>Ship of Theseus \u2013 Realignment Vector \u2013 Typical members are: Prometheans, demons and Sin-Eaters. Joins to them Free Council, Carthian Movement, Ordo Dracul, Iron Masters, Spring Court and Network Zero.</li> <li>Zero Hour \u2013 Realignment Vector \u2013 Typical members are: Forsaken werewolves, hunters, Deviants \u2013 and members of Adamantine Arrow, Saboteurs, and Furies from Sin-Eaters.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2019, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:17:43-07:00","id":1301944,"title":"","content":"Now, let\u2019s move back to the Eastern Empire CoD setting and it\u2019s Sworns. Remember, we talk here about years 330\u20131453 A.D., mainly years 600-1100s in context of this Dark Era. It\u2019s too early for <i>Ship of Theseus</i> Sworn to exist \u2013 and at least half of groups in it are non-existing for time being ( Free Council, Carthian Movement, Ordo Dracul and Network Zero ).<br /> <br /> Because of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(Byzantine_district)\" target=\"_blank\">Themata administrative model</a>, in Byzantium there is no clear distinction between military and administrative rulings \u2013 they all follow great Strategos. As this, Zero Hour predecessor is unnecessary \u2013 all administration and military related Sworn are in massive <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortals_(Byzantine_Empire)\" target=\"_blank\">Athanatoi</a></i> Sworn. It nicely connects how Legio Mortuum was just a Wing in Camarilla, what Athanatoi are direct decedents. It does lead to Athanatoi being really massive in nominal numbers ( having most of monster groups of CoD as it\u2019s members ), but it\u2019s also rather backstabbing in feel \u2013 all that joins them is need to sustain stability of Empire and protecting it against Contagions. Once that ensured, inner fights for domination and \u2018rat race\u2019 against factions return.<br /> <br /> Without Theseus existence, most of Iron Masters and Spring Court, naturally, join Athanatoi. From non-existing (yet) Zero Hour comes Adamantine Arrows, Summer Court and Furies. Yet it\u2019s Jeremiad, after Justinian Plague, are maintain \u2018moral center\u2019 of the Sworn in Empire \u2013 Athanatoi are pointed as most of time fighting with themselves. Jeremiad have plans (connected mostly with Church ) and are more effective in enforcing them. Probably in late Empire ( probably from 12th century onward? ) from Athanatoi are spread those that will be later known as Machiavelli Gambit. Rosetta Society can easily work as it is pointed being called <i>Omphalos</i> \u2013 a bit weird is only usage of this world for more spiritual werewolves \u2013 but it\u2019s perfect for Greek-based setting of Byzantium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2019, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T21:26:05-07:00","id":1302110,"title":"","content":"Hold up. The Ship of Theseus can exist if you want them to. Hell, even if you wanna stick to the text, all you gotta do is have an earlier version of them (since the Ship of Theseus is just the current incarnation of a recurring trend across history), which is solved by giving them a cool new name. Problem solved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T09:10:33-07:00","id":1302238,"title":"","content":"I started to listen podcast about <a href=\"https://therussianhistorypodcast.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">history of Russia</a> - In <a href=\"https://therussianhistorypodcast.podbean.com/e/episode-8-kiev/\" target=\"_blank\">this episode</a> is described founding of Kiev by Vikings of Askold and Dir - and their later attack on Constantinople in 860 AD. I advise to listen whole podcast, as in it's previous episodes describe history and culture of various ethnic groups that build future various Rus kingdoms - and next conflicts with Byzantium of those, in coming centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-03-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T06:09:23-07:00","id":1303060,"title":"","content":"I started <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine%E2%80%99s-empire-kindred\">separate topic on sole society of Kindred in Byzantine Empire</a> - for official stuff and fans musings. Here are my main ideas from there:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1303051-dark-eras-byzantine\u2019s-empire-kindred?p=1303052#post1303052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>In <b>VtR</b> 2E corebook setting of Athenes ( Polis of Erabus ) is mentioning of chtonics gods vampiric priestess <i>Despoina,</i> <i>Mother of Bones</i>. She worship Echidna, mythological Mother of Monsters, so works as cult for proto-Circle of Crone in area. I would even more gladly use here, as I wanted to use some beasts crossovers \u2013 and worshipping Mother of Monsters certainly works here. 8-) So I would probably use Cult of Echidna as proto-Circle of Crone in setting, replacing Cult of Augurs, centuries before great unification. As I use Sworn from <b>Contagion Chronicle</b>, this cult will join probably <i>Omphalos</i>, predecessor to Rosetta Society, in place of CoC.</li> <li><i>Athanatoi</i>, as particular human unit idea, was created in year 970 AD. However, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theme_(Byzantine_district)\" target=\"_blank\">Themata Refrom</a>, where Byzantium was divided between between military-administrative provinces \u2013 was done in 640s and spread as idea around Empire. By 700s it was popular model or ruling in Byzantium. By 750s there was created <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagma_(military)\" target=\"_blank\">Tagma</a> military units around Empire, that were de facto long arm of Emperor. I think that creation of <i>Adamantes Athanatoi </i>as Kindred Covenant on late 690s /early 700s is okay in that context.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2019, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:44:55-07:00","id":1304030,"title":"","content":"Reading more materials from <b>Contagion Chronicle </b>previews and <b>Vampire</b> gameline, I wanted to prepare semi-final sum up how various monsters organisations are fitting the puzzle in Byzantium. We start with Plague\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sworn of Justinian</b></span><br /> <br /> In 6<sup>th</sup> century after Christ, first Plague hit Byzantium. It started vicious cycle of sickness and death that took tall of almost one third of Eastern Roman Empire, across next three centuries. And it bring Sworn to fight it.<br /> <br /> At the rules of Emperor Justinian I, in one year, from 541 to 542 \u2013 pandemic of Plague killed 40% of population of Constantinople. What mortals did not known, was that (later called ) Black Death had also supernatural dimension. Some of those that died from illness, had return to life. And then died again. And return to life. And died again. Being locked in this miserable cycle, they still spread the disease, adding next to damned army of living dead. Numbers were not enough to call the open battlefield \u2013 but those of night-dwellers races known they need to respond or the secret of their existence will be broken. They need to eradicate this sickness.<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum ruling Constantinople - joined by newly formed Legions of Damned from previous Legio Mortuum regiments - is trying to solve epidemic on it\u2019s own. Sanctified need to do this, because from over century Camarilla de facto is no more \u2013 even when few in Kindred society still use it\u2019s name. Finally, sickness pass from Rome of East \u2013 was it workings of vampires, God Machine or mages \u2013 is to this day hotly debated. Most would agree it was will of God ( or gods ).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Convention and Splitting</b></span><br /> <br /> Sensing that Death can return to Empire, Aelia Scaevola, a Nosferatu researcher with few others children of the night started secret convention of scholars to seek ways to stop the next outbreak. They found under city ancient tomb that foretold great disaster. And those researchers spill over Empire, to look clues for the secret.<br /> <br /> It was Aelia who remembered 25 years later that sigil found in tomb to come from times of Cyrus in Achaemenid Empire, twelve hundred years earlier. Mage from Cyrus times, Vishtapa, found first signs of Contagion in their country. As Scaevola was from Lance and Spear, she was versed in Scriptures \u2013 and instantly remembered the prophecy of Jeremiah about the Fall of Babylon. She spread the idea with her colleagues and soon joined by other of monsters believing that Plague of Justinian was God\u2019s Judgment \u2013 and only faith, zeal and morality can save night-dwellers and mortals from next outbreak. They quickly infiltrated the Church and lesser cults in Empire \u2013 or rather were there from beginning - looking over ways to please the God ( and gods ). <i>Jeremiad</i> Sworn were created.<br /> <br /> But not every researcher from convention of the tomb agreed with Aelia. Some mystics were looking inside their own mind and souls for answers. Mages and beasts that seen discovery and sigil from tomb looked a lot like Omphalos Stone inside Astral Space they visit routinely on their journeys. They focused on understanding it\u2019s meaning and how dreams can help cure the Plague. Both rivalry Orders of Awakened, Panscryptia and Keepers of the World, agreed ( for the first time ) on importance of Sacred Stone. Joined by Despoina, the Mother of Bones, chthonian vampires priestess of Echidna from Athens, adversary of Scaevola, they started their own group. <i>Omphalos</i> Sworn were created.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Athanatoi</b></span><br /> <br /> Those two Sworn groups were unchallenged by few decades, where last remnants of Camarilla were trying to rise up in Night Society, however without success. Curse of Hasdrubal hanged on everything that originated from Rome itself. Ayzebel, sister-in-law to Carthages general that Curse take it\u2019s name \u2013 the same women that became creator of those that in modern night we call Cryptocracy \u2013 was Embraced and joined Camarilla in Eternal City and strive to end Contagion in Italy with like-minded. She felt with the Senex itself, but her disciple went to Byzantium with Constantine The Great. Chaos in the city did not let them took their roots. Until Senex was no more. Kindred needed new system of ruling \u2013 mortals in Empire gave them.<br /> <br /> Themata province system was created in the mid-7th century in the aftermath of the Slavic invasion of the Balkans and Muslim conquests of parts of Byzantine territory. It overturned older Roman system the strict division of civil and military offices. With new ruling system forming on their eyes, disciples of Ayzebel went for power and to control Plague, for the good of Empire. New group stated they want to stable society and give victories with Contagion for the Byzantium. They become nation sensitive leaders monsters. At the dawn of year 700s. they called themselves <i>Athanatoi</i>, Immortals. New Sworn were created in Byzantium.<br /> <br /> 10<sup>th</sup> century, mortals elite military under this conspiracy would call themselves the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sworn and False of Byzantine Empire</b></span><br /> In brackets are names for modern counterparts of those groups. Historical factions use mechanics the same as their nowdays decendents.<br /> <br /> <b>Sworn of this Era:</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jeremiad-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Jeremiad</b></a> - <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Religious and morality-centred monsters. Connected to mortal ( future ) Orthodox Church. After 6th century and it\u2019s Plague of Justinian \u2013 most influential Sworn faction. <b>Typical members:</b> Lancea et Sanctum, beasts, hunters, mummies and Prometheans. Joins them Integrators, Hunters in Darkness and Lucifuge.</div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><b><i>Athanatoi </i></b>(<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-cryptocracy-contagion-chronicle/\" target=\"_blank\">Cryptocracy</a>) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Monsters sustaining government and rules in Empire. They are remnants from original Camarilla of Rome \u2013 and future part of Invictus. Connected mostly to Themata province system. <b>Typical members:</b> Athanatoi Convenat ( rests of Camarilla, future Invictus ), beasts, demons, mages and vampires. Join to them Adamantine Arrow, Blood Talons, Iron Masters, Storm Lords, Winter, Spring &amp; Summer Courts, Maa-Kep, and Undertakers from Sin-Eaters. </div></div> </div> </div></li> <li><b><i>Omphalos</i></b> (Rosetta Society) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Researches of sacred and secret, they name comes both title for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omphalos\" target=\"_blank\">mythological stone letting to communicate directly with gods</a> \u2013 and Astral Space barrier that many mages and beasts find in their journeys. <b>Typical members: </b>mages from Keepers of the Word and Pancryptiates Orders ( in 12<sup>th</sup> century they merge into modern Mysterium, but in this Dark Eras they compete inside Sworn ), beasts, demons, changelings, hunters and werewolves. Joins too them Bone Shadows, Circle of the Crone, Mekhet vampires, Sesha-Hebsu, Mourners from Sin-Eaters and Tammuz. </div></div> </div> </div></li> </ul><b>False of this Era:</b><br /> <br /> \u00b7<b><i>Horde</i> </b>(Naglfar\u2019s Army) \u2013 <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Literal \u2018barbarians at the gates\u2019 \u2013 and on the inside. Over centuries, Easter Roman Empire had many enemies \u2013 Huns, Khazars, Arabs, Vikings, Ottamans and many, many others. Each of this groups was coming with next war that could \u2018end the world\u2019. What was joining them was secret support of night-dwellers, wanting to tear down Empire, once and for all. However Horde was not only on the outside \u2013 but was infiltrating Night Society in the inside. From the times of Ancient Rome, at least handful of monsters were doing their own \u2018Saturnalia\u2019, preparing for the end of world. With enemies on the outside and inside \u2013 Byzantine Empire finally was no more. In 900\u2019s Horde dogma mixed with Vikings legends of Ragnarok \u2013 and modern Naglfar\u2019s Army was created from there.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-10-2019, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T01:11:08-07:00","id":1309136,"title":"","content":"I create second Byzantium Contagion Outbreak - Iconclasm, Contagion of Being. It's creation is formation of 700s and onward Sworn factions. Here are early drafts of Jeremiad and Athantoi in them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Sworn</b></span><br /> <br /> Sworn see Iconoclasm Contagion as possible end of their living \u2013 or at least history. They strife to not forget about their comrades and their own secrets.<br /> <br /> <b>700-900s</b><br /> <br /> In first years of Contagion, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1304030#post1304030\">newly founded Sworn in Byzantine Empire</a> did not even noticed it. It fell between the cracks, as the whole alliance was looking for the signs of next Plague of Justinian outbreak in that time. Unfortunately, disease has settled within Eastern Roman Empire. From then, it was mostly crisis management and hoping to cure the patients. However, each of Sworn groups tried, from time to time, some revolutionary way for stopping the disease. After few decades they observed that because the Contagion was sourced from Iconoclasm and destruction of the visage \u2013 the way to stop it was to created many visages of the patient and then to mark the worship of image on it. To say that those practiced seemed to look heretical, even to eyes of Iconludes, was to put it mildly. And then Sworn still looked for other ways stopping this outbreak.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jeremiad</span></b><br /> <br /> Connected most with the Easter Church itself, the Penitents are in the centre of Iconclams Contagion.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b><br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum is doubling down on separation of worship in Empire, leading to their members distance themselves from the center of infections. Seeing how this Contagion is striving from destruction of icons, Sanctified in Jeremiad are hoarding holy images and statues, persevering them, so the new sources of disease would not spread more. They also most ardently worship them, to undo existing infections.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves</b><br /> <br /> Hunters in Darkness and Fire-Touched inside Church\u2019s holy places are defending icons before destruction with their own claws. They know that once Contagion will set in area, they are first to get the worst of it. It also lead to unusual alliance \u2013 Hosts also do not want to be in area of this Plague. As both physical and ephemeral beings like <i>Meninna </i>and <i>Izidakh</i> \u2013 they know they are most venerable to the gruesome effects of it. Hosts separated from their species simply decomposes and die.<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts</b><br /> <br /> Begotten in Church are trying to preach \u2013 by word and Nightmares they send \u2013 that you must see and confront what you are afraid off. And by this, images helps us prepare to life we lead. Often, it ends with unofficial, private visages of mythological horrors that haunts particular painter or sculptor \u2013 but it sustain particular beast from Contagion if she became infected.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Athanatoi (Cryptocracy) </b></span><br /> Athanatoi, as predecessors of Cryptocracy we know now, try to fight with problem systematically. It\u2019s their secret support in in the elites of society that lead to support Iconludes in stopping the destructions of icons. Whenever they can, Immortals try to hijack commands that leads to more damages and possible spread of Contagion. It\u2019s Athanatoi influence on the Emperor\u2019s Court that maybe ended Iconclams madness. Started from vampires Covenant mission to secure Empire, movement quickly spread to whole new Sworn faction.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b><br /> <br /> Themata province system was created in the mid-7th century in the aftermath of the Slavic invasion of the Balkans and Muslim conquests of parts of Byzantine territory. It overturned older Roman system the strict division of civil and military offices. With new ruling system forming on their eyes, disciples of Ayzebel from Cathage went for power and to control Plague, for the good of Empire. New group stated they want to stable society and give victories with Contagion for the Byzantium. They become nation sensitive leaders monsters. At the dawn of year 700s. they called themselves <i>Athanatoi</i>, Immortals. New Sworn were created in Byzantium.<br /> <br /> <i>Athanatoi</i> Covenant of vampires is rising sect, building on the remnants of Senex that was powerful only 3 centuries earlier. They are following the Oaths of various <i>Strategoi </i>to <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ruled over a council of <i>Prisci</i>, the eldest members of each Kindred clan. Reconnecting old infrastructures of crumbled Senex to new conspiracy under Night Emperor, they usher new Vampiric Empire inside Easter Roman Empire, with moral support of Sanctified. Set on the idea of feudalism and securing the stability of Both Empires, after centuries of unrest in lands, many neonates are flocking to the new faction \u2013 counting also on the power and influence in coming centuries.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves</b><br /> <br /> ( For the Uratha section of Athantoi, I use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a> idea for Themisine Protectorate of Pure. )<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1166388#post1166388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the late 3rd Century AD the Romulan Protectorate is stretched thin across the world, and the Magna Mater, huge, bloated and self cannibalizing, is raving mad. The Protectorate separates with the Roman Empire. This has the fortunate side-effect of quelling the Magna Mater's agony for a brief respite in the local hisil. The Eastern Protectorate is led by a more equitable arrangement of Fire-Touched and Ivory Claws, with the Poenii claiming authority over all matters spiritual, and the Claws over mortal affairs - much like in the Romulan Protectorate, but with more power and recognition granted to the Fire Touched.<br /> <br /> This new Protectorate is called the Themisine Protectorate. The Fire-Touched, with authority from the gods, and their Ur-Father, and Father Wolf himself, and touched with divine fevers and insight, guide the more mortal policies enacted by the Ivory Claws. Together they act in (supposed) balance. They have no Magna Mater to appease, or contend with - packs of Uratha squabble over territory until the Protectorate is threatened by packs of 'barbarian' Forsaken. The Themisines bargain heavily with the local Predator Kings, whom they dubbed 'Naturae', in order to combat the rising Forsaken threat, and the constant threat of rogue spirits bolstered by beliefs from dozens of nations and all seeing an opportunity to become the new Protectorate's 'Mater'.<br /> <br /> Over the decades the three tribes of Pure further divide the Themisine Protectorate among triadic councils - the Horae. Each council holds three Pure - one of each tribe - and each of the three councils is led by a different tribe.<br /> <br /> The First Council is led by a Fire Touched in the seat of 'Xarpo', with The Ivory Claw in the seat of 'Thallo' and the Predator King in the seat of 'Auxo'.<br /> The Second Council is led by an Ivory Claw in the seat of 'Eirene', with the Predator King in the seat of 'Dike' and the Fire Touched in the seat of 'Eunomia'<br /> The Third Council is led by a Predator King in the Seat of 'Orthosie', witht he Fire Touched in the seat of 'Euporie' and the Ivory Claw in the seat of 'Pherusa'<br /> <br /> These three councils shared authority over the Themisine Protectorate, supported by a Fourth Council of Nemeses. This council held limited authority - it was convened to lead Themesine packs to war, and membership was fluid. The Atropos seat was for the Predator King, the Clotho seat was given to the Ivory Claw, and the Lachesis seat was given to the Fire Touched. In times of great conflict multiple 'Fourth Councils' were created to cover different fronts, and only rarely was any 'Fourth' council completely filled. Most often, one tribe would fill their seat and take command of the local packs while another tribe would take command elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Themisine Protectorate is looking for the stability of Empire and spirit world. Iconoclasm Contagion is clearly threaten it, so it should be eliminated. With the help of few Iron Masters joining their ranks in Athanoi, Protectorate is trying to solve spiritual sickness by edicts and commands in Themata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2019, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T06:30:24-07:00","id":1343978,"title":"","content":"Great sum up and funny video on the history of Byzantine Empire - from year 300 till 700 AD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's generally the summary how Byzantium come to being and how it diverged from original Rome. I suspect follow up in the few weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7LZbSbatwSg\" data-code=\"7LZbSbatwSg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7LZbSbatwSg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:41:39-07:00","id":1344963,"title":"","content":"I started separate topic for the Constantinopole proper setting - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1344875-dark-eras-fan-constantinople-%E2%80%93-early-medieval-istanbul-turkey-%E2%80%93-700-%E2%80%93-1000-ad\">it's here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:38:44-07:00","id":1345401,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Vampires Government \u2013 Night Emperor, Patriarch and Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <br /> Kindred society of Constantinople is governed like that of mortal \u2013 just much more stable. When in living Empire, ruler can be change for complete stranger in one, two decades \u2013 undead are much more certain in their choices. Mostly because they are virtually immortal. If he is clever in his politics, new <i>Dominus Noctis Imperator</i> ( Great Night Imperator ) is chosen once in few centuries when previous one is going to Torpor, from Prisci Council \u2013 leaders of Clans in city, and by this, in Empire. New Imperator is appointing now <i>Stratoegoi</i> ( sing. <i>Strategos </i>) \u2013 generals in the field, to look over his matters for him in Empire, under sacred Oaths to him. All other them are watched if they making will of God by the<i> Patriarch of the Damned</i>, <i>Vicar of Longinus</i>, <i>Archbishop of Constantinople. </i>Sanctified Patriarch and Imperator rule almost as co-princes, with Imperator taking matters of world and Patriarch those of souls.<br /> <br /> Within city, Kindred are divided into <i>thema</i>, administrative groups (usually divided by lineage) with specific responsibilities to the Kindred government who gained specific rights in return, usually in regard to where they might haven and feed. The <i>Mystikoi</i>, a line of Gangrel monks, serve as scribes and historians, for example, and are given the right to feed from the city\u2019s monastic population.<br /> <br /> Nowadays rules of Imperator and Prisci Council ( 700-1000 AD ) is result of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plague_of_Justinian\" target=\"_blank\">Justinian Plague</a> of 541 ( with it\u2019s repeated resurgences till 750 AD ) \u2013 called centuries later Black Death. With as high as 40% mortality rate in Empire, it took many of humans supplies and networks of older Roman Elders \u2013 leading to their downfall or even Final Death. With humans dying en masse and normal dead returning to \u2018life\u2019 \u2013 Kindred needed change of rules. With old Patriarch lost in tumult and Prisci Council finally dead, vampires looked for new leaders. It came with <i>Ventranis</i> \u2013 previous barbarians hordes leader from West that became general in Days Emperor armies. He with few others Ancillae helped new appointed Patriarch Ivonius enforced order in Plague stricken Constantinopole. Following traditions of living Eastern Roman Empire, he was anointed Dominus Noctis Imperator by Ivonius \u2013 and start it\u2019s rules as King ( or rather, Emperor ) of Night in Reigning City. He appointed his helpers as Prisci that now advise him in ranks of Athanatoi. Researchers in Imperial Library whispers that they found legend about Imperator\u2019s name giver \u2013 Ven \u2013 being connected to stories of Troy and creation of Julii Clan of old\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dominus Noctis Imperator \u2013 Ventranis</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: \u2018Ven\u2019 ( future Ventrue )</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>482 CE ( same as birth of Emperor Justinian )<br /> <br /> Centuries ago, Ventranis was commander of one of next barbarian armies that lead siege on Constantinople. What was not known \u2013 he already was vampire of ancient noble and leaders Clan spread inside \u2018uncivilised\u2019 lands. Some rumours said he is related to Julii, somehow. His strategic mind and acumen lead him to become Day Emperors Justinian general, helping, in the end, to defend Byzantium. He hid his vampiric condition as \u2018foreign customs of his people\u2019 \u2013 and led small politics in Empire. Then came the Plague and everything changed. Without Prisci Council and with old Patriarch missing, there was chaos. Ventranis took matters in his own hands, helped new Archbishop Iovinus, collected willing and able to bring order with him in the City. It took half century, but they done it. They become next Prisci Council and in next 50 years, Ventranis is crowned first Dominus Noctis Imperator. ( Circa year 650 AD. )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Patriarch of the Damned \u2013 Iovinus</b></span><br /> <b>Clan: Daeva</b><br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Ag\u00eda Lans ( gr. Lancea Sanctum )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>532 CE ( Start of building Hagia Sophia )<br /> <br /> Iovinus was mesmerizing Roman priest of Greek heritage. He was observed by previous Patriarch, Alexander, from his teenage years. Vicar of Longinus even tried to romance and tempt young cleric \u2013 which he succeed. But only after Nike riots in 532 AD Alexander understood that he need a Child to take after him. When the Day Emperor in same year started building of Hagia Sophia, Alexander knew it was sign. On his 33rd birthdays, just like his Sire, Iovinus died to be reborn in Longinus. He only had 9 years of his undead existence when Alexander disappeared with first wave of Plague. Confused and unready to rule, he probably would lose the power \u2013 if not help from Ventranis. Together they lead order and stability \u2013 and controlled Plague in Constantinopole Kindred society. They\u2019re alliance lead domain to prosper \u2013 and let Patriarch to look over the matters of soul \u2013 so, Ivonius crowned Ventranis as Dominus Noctis Imperator.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prisci Council</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gangrel Priscus \u2013 Vigilius</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Gangrel<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>585 CE ( Slavs invasion of Constantinopole )<br /> <br /> Vigilius was one of defenders of City before Slavs. He died with name of the Christ on his mouth. And later awoken to the night. He was resurrected by one of \u2018barbarian demons\u2019. He slew his original pagan Sire and drove to the Legions of Damned knight order. However, seeing as Legion is too much theological fanatics and much less real army \u2013 he looked for inspirations. It came when Plague once more hit the Constantinople, and Ventranis gone to organise help and fight with returned dead. Vigilius joined future Imperator and advised to him creating more secular forces of knights to defend Queen of Cities, with Legions being less and less real force. Together, they started what would become Athnatoi, laying Oaths to new appointed Imperator of Night.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mekhet Priscus \u2013 Eugenia</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Mekhet<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>543 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Eugenia was daughter of Byzantine noble. She could not go to Church run university, but learned all she could as independent Roman noblewomen. She devoured ancient scrolls and books on medicine and anatomy. If she was not women, she could become doctor. And then Plague came. She tried to fight it on streets. She tried to save her family when father brought sickness from the next military campaign. Finally, she did not save them - and she was dead. She awoke in the mass grave of Plague victims, from what she crawled up. Her Sire has prepared her and pointed her to save human and Kindred from Plague. And so she started to fight it, with all her knowledge and might. When Ventranis called for help, she gladly joined him. For the good of Empire \u2013 and it\u2019s people!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nosferatu Priscus \u2013 Skolikas ( Worm )</b></span><br /> <b>Clan</b>: Nosferatu<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Athanatoi ( future Invictus )<br /> <b>Embraced: </b>541 CE ( Justinian Plague )<br /> <br /> Man called Skolikas was on of first victims of the Plague. The so called \u2018King of Beggars\u2019, he was finest fixer in the low strata of society. Of course, he was one of first to come in contact with sick and leppers. He was dying by days. Then his Mother give him choice of dying in pain \u2013 or too live forever with marks of disease. He choose later. He bears his Plague marks with pride \u2013 but he really want to end suffering of poor and outcast. He helped Ventranis \u2013 and now make sure that people on the low end of social ladder will also have voice. His voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T02:42:50-08:00","id":1350411,"title":"","content":"I started to listen <b><a href=\"https://thehistoryofbyzantium.com/\" target=\"_blank\">\u2018History of Byzantium\u2019</a></b> podcast, connecting my interests in Roman Empire, early Medieval Times and Vikings. Byzantium \u2013 called Rome of East \u2013 or often as Constantinople was successor of antiquity Roman Empire by over millennium. But not the pagan city of predecessor \u2013 but rather first Christian empire of the world, now being called Istanbul in Turkey. 8-)<br /> <br /> Introduction of podcast - <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-f8vtm-15817ca\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-f8vtm-15817ca</a><br /> <br /> Change from Roman Empire to Byzantine Empire - <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-5ik7s-15817c9\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-5ik7s-15817c9</a><br /> <br /> Constantinople \\ city of Byzantium description \u2013 and how it\u2019s citizens lived there. <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-u359k-ffa585\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-u359k-ffa585</a><br /> <br /> Plague of Justinian of 542 A.D. \u2013 most important event for the fan setting I build for CoD below - <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-zqmb4-15f05ec\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-zqmb4-15f05ec</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T08:29:22-08:00","id":1351289,"title":"","content":"<br /> Preparing the play setting and listening to History of Byzantium podcast \u2013 I understand I cannot cling to one Dark Era setting for the whole Empire stretch. So I will divide it into 4 smaller periods subchapters, with proper settings ideas, based on general divide on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Empire\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia of Empire</a>. Because of historical implications, each new Era will be based on information from previous one.<br /> <br /> <b>Mini-Eras</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Dawn of Byzantium</i> - End of Western Empire and Justinian dynasty (480 \u2013 626)</li> <li><i>Shrinking Empire</i> - Shrinking borders and Macedonian dynasty (626 \u2013 1025)</li> <li><i>Broken Eagle</i> - Komnenian dynasty and the Crusades (1025 \u2013 1204)</li> <li><i>Fall of Byzantium</i> \u2013 Up to conquer by Ottomans (1204 - 1475)</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-27-2019, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T01:30:55-08:00","id":1351809,"title":"","content":"I start to do First Draft of proper PDF product. Here is opening Table of Contet for the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://imgur.com/6mOyIgE\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/6mOyIgE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T01:32:20-08:00","id":1351810,"title":"","content":"And here is first version of Introduction subchapter...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Introduction</b></span><br /> <br /> This book is work of heart from fans of <b>Chronicles of Darkness </b>and history. It\u2019s fan expansion of canon of <b>CofD</b> gamelines as <b>Dark Eras</b> setting in times of great empire on the East \u2013 Byzantium, the Rome of East. All shown here materials are <i>not <b>CofD</b> canon </i>\u2013 but they derived and are based on canon sources. Many times I point to official materials from what those ideas spring. Here is short list of those product that maybe needed for you to use some of concepts inside this book.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness products</b></span><ul><li><b><i>Contagion Chronicles</i></b> \u2013 One of most impactful struggles that Byzantines needed to confront was Plague of Justinian that returned to Empire for over two centuries, shaping its history to what we know today. However, there were also other hazards for the peace of nation \u2013 one of them was Iconoclasm conflicts inside of Empire. Both of those events were having supernatural repercussions as two Contagion strains that worked on the Empire. <i>Contagion Chronicles</i> will let you better understand those phenomena \u2013 and aspects of many monster races fighting with repercussions of those in Eastern Roman Empire, in cross-races factions, known as Sworn and False.</li> <li><b><i>Dark Eras </i></b><b>products</b> \u2013 List is a bit long, as this fan setting connects them in Byzantium times, stretching over 1000 years of history:</li> </ul><ul><li><i>After the Fall,</i><b> Dark Eras 1 </b><b>\u2013 DtD </b>era about Byzantine Empire after Ottomans defeated it, from 1453 AD</li> <li><i>Forsaken by Rome</i>, <b>Dark Eras 1 Companion \u2013 WtF </b>era about Roman Uratha in 1<sup>st</sup> century.</li> <li><i>1001 Nights, </i><b>Dark Eras 2 \u2013 VtR</b> and<b> BtP </b>setting about Abbasid Caliphate in Islamic Golden Age (750 to 1258)</li> <li><b>Requiem for Rome</b>: <b>Fall of Camarilla </b>\u2013 Precursor to <b>Dark Eras</b> settings line itself, it marks vampires society from the time of fall of Rome to rules of Justinian in 532 AD.</li> <li><b>VtR: Ancient Mysteries </b>\u2013 Book for <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, full of historical settings.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Inspirations</b></span><br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://thehistoryofbyzantium.com/\" target=\"_blank\">History of Byzantium podcast</a></b> \u2013 One of best source on constant narrative of Byzantine Empire, from its start as Eastern part of Roman Empire in 4<sup>th</sup> century \u2013 till it\u2019s fall under Ottomans in 15<sup>th</sup> century. Great journey that will show you all the Byzantine history, intertwined and in context of previous and later events. I highly recommend it to you! Source - <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/podcast-detail/dr8qc-2f281/The-History-of-Byzantium-Podcast\" target=\"_blank\">HoB on Podbean</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Mini-Eras</b></span><br /> <br /> Byzantium Empire history is too much for only one <b>Dark Eras</b> setting. In order to encompass it all, we need to divide it into 4 smaller periods subchapters, with proper settings ideas and materials. Because of historical implications, each new Era will be based on information from previous one.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><i>Dawn of Byzantium</i> - End of Western Empire and Justinian dynasty (480 \u2013 626)</li> <li><i>Shrinking Empire</i> - Shrinking borders and Macedonian dynasty (626 \u2013 1025)</li> <li><i>Broken Eagle</i> - Komnenian dynasty and the Crusades (1025 \u2013 1204)</li> <li><i>Fall of Byzantium</i> \u2013 Up to conquer by Ottomans (1204 - 1475)</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-30-2019, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T13:44:42-08:00","id":1352050,"title":"","content":"First, I want to thanks users that helped me on this project! Many thanks to: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2291\" data-vbnamecard=\"2291\">Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3523\" data-vbnamecard=\"3523\">Spencer from The Hills</a> - without you guys, we would not have all we have now in it. I want to hear from you what do you think about now ready text.<br /> <br /> Second, I finalized First Draft of 1/3 of the Dark Era - Introduction and <i>Dawn of Byzantium</i> chapter. It's probably the most informative and rest half of mechanical and setting changes will be in <i>next</i> chapter - ( so if you don't see your idea, it will probably be in next part ) - but it lays groundwork for the setting and points to main elements like Sworn, False, new Covenants, new Protectorate or new Orders. I also analyze life in Byzantium in 6th century, hoping to show how it was different from Western Roman times of official Dark Eras to this date. I hope that you like what you read - and point me where it should be improved.<br /> <br /> Here is first part of First Draft <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> -<br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/nkr50m0h3nq8yli/DE%20Byznatine%20Empire%20Final%20PDF.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/nkr50m0h3n...20PDF.pdf?dl=0</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T19:40:09-08:00","id":1352504,"title":"","content":"When you uncover that <b>Game of Thrones</b> is great inspiration for stories in Byzantium! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here is new Inspirations sum-up I added to Dark Era drafts and sidebar on eunuch in Empire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><i>Game of Thrones</i></b> TV series / <b><i>Song of Ice and Fire</i></b> books series \u2013 Epic fantasy series that have a lot of common themes with Byzantine Empire history. Multinational medieval country that is successor to great empire that conquered half of then known world. The state undergoing constant trial from plague that can easily be God\u2019s Judgment ( Plague of Justinian / Black Death and hordes of undead ), torn apart by struggles of noble families that could practically be independent kingdoms (dynasties of specific provinces) or rebels taking power from a ruling dynasty - and then clearing the country of the descendants of the previous one. There are also eunuchs possessing powerful influences in the palace, an unusual substance that allows you to burn every enemy (Greek Fire) or barbaric peoples of the Great Steppe that you have to tame - or get along with them. In this Dark Era we go a step further and say that <i>among</i> real world Plague victims is new undead threat. Both TV series and book series nicely show us what can happen then to protagonists.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Eunuchs</b></span><br /> <br /> One of unusual traditions of the Byzantine Empire was more and more important role of eunuchs in day-to-day life. Banned practice of castration in early centuries in country itself, it was very popular to get one slave for your nobility household, from the boarders outside of state. Sometimes, poor families inside the empire made the illegal procedure to ensure better life for boys not fit to live from field. Eunuchs were valued as not aggressive, sexual safe servants, with no family and work driven. With coming centuries, more and more respect was given to them. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narses\" target=\"_blank\">Narses</a> ( 476 to 573 ) was eunuch important to ruler Justinian \u2013 he was one of his closest advisors, later general and province governor ( exarch ). It was official that Emperor Chamberlain position could only be for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-03-2019, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T13:44:28-08:00","id":1360945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1300673#post1300673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </